Description:
  Adds a tool to the app's MCP server, in app/models/mcp/tools/app.rb.
  Needs maquina:mcp.

  Writes the tool's JSON Schema into DEFINITIONS, a method stub into
  Mcp::Tools::App that raises "not implemented yet", and with --write the
  name into WRITE_TOOLS (so a read-only token gets 403) with
  readOnlyHint: false. Generates test/models/mcp/tools/NAME_test.rb: the
  tool is listed, a missing required argument is -32602, a read-only token
  is refused (--write), and a skipped cross-user test to fill in. Running it
  again for the same name changes nothing.

  Arguments are name:type, with ? for optional. Types: string, integer,
  number, boolean, and enum[a,b] (a string limited to those values). Quote
  them in zsh, where ? and [] are glob characters.

  Afterwards it lists what is left to write: the description the model
  reads, the method body and the cross-user test.

Options:
  --write   The tool changes data: it needs the write scope
  --quiet   Suppress the list of items to finish

Examples:
  rails g maquina:mcp_tool list_posts 'status:enum[draft,published]?' 'limit:integer?'
  rails g maquina:mcp_tool publish_post id:integer --write
